the exact same name, parameter types and return type as in the Android docs
(https://developer.android.com/reference), or the app will crash when it reaches that call.
Constants (like Gravity.CENTER) must have the same value as the real one, since the compiler copies it.

Format: each "// == <path>" line starts a new Java file. Build.java cuts this file apart at those lines
and compiles each piece as if it were a file at <path>. Everything above the first marker is ignored.

